    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Compound climate events",
    "problem": "Traditional risk assessment methods underestimate climate risk by considering hazards in isolation, failing to capture the amplified impacts of compound events where multiple, interacting physical processes combine to cause extreme weather.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a bottom-up, impact-centric risk assessment framework that starts by identifying combinations of climate drivers and hazards causing significant impacts, in order to better understand and project the risks from such complex compound events.",
    "task": "The task is to improve projections of future climate risk by proposing a framework that analyzes \"compound events,\" where multiple interacting climate drivers and hazards combine to cause extreme impacts, overcoming the underestimation of risk from traditional single-hazard assessments.",
